  "spectral_counterexample": "m43,P69263,Q70163,N4859699869 with literal least-prime selector and projected base2 gamma3896048378. Actual canonical collisions in BOTH fields and full norm zero, but phi(x) unit for EVERY scalar modulo N.",
  "proof_mechanism": "Actual degree42 companion-pencil determinant, certified by 43 direct field determinants each; explicit Frobenius remainders and full Bezout identities gcd(phi_p,X^p-X)=1 in both certified prime fields. Independent source/identity reconstruction and byte-identical certificate regeneration.",
  "finite_scope": "ONE actual counterexample refutes universal finite-input forcing for THIS phi. Not an infinite avoidance family, asymptotic operation bound, or refutation of an expressly sufficiently-large-only theorem. Other determinants/operators remain possible.",
  "shortrow_theorem": "Actual fixed low-digit-dependent per-tag short pairs form a cap on u^2=n*a*t. Elementary projective incidence gives energy<=4m^(5/2), high-digit raw sum<=6m^(7/2), selector loss O(K_*M^6/lambda). Polylog menus retain actual majority with GLOBAL k^2T=soft Omega(m^(3/2)).",
  "shortrow_scope": "One native low-digit-dependent selected row per tag, signed a preserved; not all intermediate rays or high-digit-adaptive choices. Global no-wrap only. Representation bound, not operation lower bound or query acquisition.",
  "reflection_scope": "Exact opposite-tag carry and finite reflection identities; on stated global branch reflected multiplier cannot be q^k with |k|<=ell/2 for common intervals ell>=m^2. Only the single short-endpoint correction recipe excluded.",
  "verification_scope": "Three exact stdlib generators in clean directory plus independent portable checker. No new Lean declaration/build or overall factoring exponent.",
  "missing_work": "Restriction-stable soft O(m) sufficient factor query; full bit/controller and Lean sixth-rate composition.",
